## Next action

Phase 2 has started from the hand off below. Step one: results/probe.json carries a section for
Phase 2 (the libraries on PyPI, the two weights pinned in config/models.yaml, Kaggle and Databricks
answered or not, R with the survival package), and the model gate is scoped: model libraries only
under packages/models and kaggle/, the ONNX runtime also under packages/api, and no model provider
client or agent framework anywhere. Step two: evaluation/phase2_plan.yaml and config/models.yaml are
hashed into evaluation/registration.json as the models stage, after the Phase 1 stages and without
moving their hash, before any model exists. Next: step three, the training set builder on the as-of
engine, with the leakage test on the sets. Step three: scripts/build_sets.py writes the sets
(data/sets, rebuilt from the lake, never committed) and results/models/sets.json with their digests:
{{ v("models.sets.train.rows") }} train, {{ v("models.sets.development.rows") }} development, {{ v("models.sets.test.rows") }} test and {{ v("models.sets.shadow.rows") }} shadow rows. Next: step four,
the fill floors, after the change request that starts the exploitation population when KEV could
first list a CVE within 180 days.

## Open problems

- Releases and tags come only from Ajay: this session cannot create a release or start a workflow
  that creates one, and its git access cannot push a tag, so v0.2.0 is pushed from his machine.
- Kaggle and Databricks secrets are not set yet. Without the Kaggle pair, step eight takes its CPU
  fallback; without the Databricks pair, the registry uses the file store.
- The schedules fire hours late and less often than they ask: the hourly fetch has run a few times
  a day since 12 November, and the daily fetch and lake build several hours after their times. The
  newest lake release changes with each hourly run until the next daily one, so the committed
  numbers come from the release before it (DECISIONS.md, 13 November).
- config/filers.yaml, as the first fetch wrote it, holds the listed filers without their record
  counts. The lake types the other assigners from the CVE List bronze, and the fetcher writes the
  counts again when the CNA list next changes (DECISIONS.md, 13 November).
- k6 cannot be downloaded on the build machine; the load test runs the same scenario on httpx
  (DECISIONS.md, 12 November).
- The legacy CSV dates a CVE outside the serving slice by its advisories, since the slice holds no
  record for it.

